<title>USA: Cooper Cos plans acquisition.</title>
<headline>Cooper Cos plans acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cooper Cos Inc on Monday said it has agreed to acquire from Wesley-Jessen Corp the Natural Touch line of opaque contact lenses for sale in the United States.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were undisclosed.  Cooper's unit, CooperVision Inc, will market these products.  The deal is subject to the approval of the Federal Trade Commission.</p>
<p>Natural Touch products can change the appearance of the color of the eye.  The proposed purchase furthers CooperVision's strategy of providing specialty contact lenses.</p>
</text>
